package Libraries.Game.Collision.Narrowphase

use Libraries.Compute.Vector3
use Libraries.Game.Collision.LocalCollisionPoints3D
use Libraries.Game.Collision.CollisionPointsResult3D
use Libraries.Game.Collision.PhysicsPosition3D
use Libraries.Game.Collision.Shapes.Triangle

/*
TriangleCollider3D is the parent of the colliders that test a shape against a
single triangle, such as a sphere, box or cylinder against one triangle of a
terrain. It holds what they all share: the triangle in world space, a clipper
for building contact polygons, and the one place where a contact is turned
into the form CollisionPointsResult3D expects.

A collision between two items has an item A and an item B, and
CollisionPointsResult3D:AddCollisionPoint expects a normal pointing from B
toward A, a point on B, and a depth that is negative when the two overlap.
The triangle can be either item. Terrain makes the triangle item A, so that is
the usual case, but a collider may be called the other way around. Rather
than each collider working this out, they all describe a contact the same
way, by a normal pointing from the triangle toward the shape, a point on the
shape, and the separation, and AddContact converts it.

The triangle colliders never call RefreshCollisionPoints. A concave shape such
as terrain tests many triangles against the same collision, and refreshes the
points once when it has tested them all.

A collider is used in three steps: Begin, to say where contacts go and which
item the triangle is; LoadTriangle, to load the triangle; and then the
collider's own collision action, which calls AddContact for each contact.
*/
class TriangleCollider3D
    TriangleGeometry3D geometry
    ContactClipper3D clipper

    LocalCollisionPoints3D collisionPoints = undefined
    CollisionPointsResult3D result = undefined
    boolean swapped = false
    number triangleMargin = 0

    // Reused by AddContact.
    Vector3 reportedNormal
    Vector3 reportedPoint

    /*
    This action gets the collider ready to report contacts for one collision.
    Attribute: Parameter collisionPoints The collision's stored contact points.
    Attribute: Parameter result Where contacts are reported. It must already be initialized with the collision's two items.
    Attribute: Parameter shapeIsItemA False when the triangle is item A, which is how terrain calls it, and true when the other shape is item A.
    */
    action Begin(LocalCollisionPoints3D collisionPoints, CollisionPointsResult3D result, boolean shapeIsItemA)
        me:collisionPoints = collisionPoints
        me:result = result
        me:swapped = shapeIsItemA
        result:SetCollisionPoints(collisionPoints)
    end

    /*
    This action loads a triangle, moving its corners into the world using the
    given transform, and takes its margin from the triangle.
    */
    action LoadTriangle(Triangle triangle, PhysicsPosition3D transform)
        geometry:Load(triangle, transform)
        triangleMargin = triangle:GetMargin()
    end

    /*
    This action loads a triangle whose corners are already in world space,
    with the given margin.
    */
    action LoadTriangle(Vector3 a, Vector3 b, Vector3 c, number margin)
        geometry:Load(a, b, c)
        triangleMargin = margin
    end

    /*
    This action returns the loaded triangle.
    */
    action GetGeometry returns TriangleGeometry3D
        return geometry
    end

    /*
    This action returns the clipper the collider uses to build contact
    polygons.
    */
    action GetClipper returns ContactClipper3D
        return clipper
    end

    /*
    This action returns how thick a shell is added around the triangle. The
    triangle is treated as if it were this much thicker on both sides and
    this much wider past every edge, which is what the general collision test
    does with a triangle's margin.
    */
    action GetTriangleMargin returns number
        return triangleMargin
    end

    /*
    This action returns true when the other shape, not the triangle, is item A.
    */
    action IsSwapped returns boolean
        return swapped
    end

    /*
    This action returns how far apart two shapes may be and still have a
    contact recorded. Contacts farther apart than this are not kept.
    */
    action GetContactThreshold returns number
        return collisionPoints:GetCollisionBreakingThreshold()
    end

    /*
    This action reports one contact. The contact is described the same way by
    every triangle collider, and is converted here to the form that
    CollisionPointsResult3D expects, based on which item the triangle is.

    When the triangle is item A, the normal from B toward A points from the
    shape toward the triangle, and the point on B is the point on the shape.
    When the shape is item A, the normal points from the triangle toward the
    shape, and the point on B is the matching point on the triangle, found by
    moving back across the gap. Either way, the point on A that
    CollisionPointsResult3D works out, the point on B plus the normal times
    the depth, is the other side of the same contact.
    Attribute: Parameter normalTowardShape The unit normal pointing from the triangle toward the shape.
    Attribute: Parameter pointOnShape The contact point on the shape's surface, in world space.
    Attribute: Parameter separation How far apart the shape and the triangle are along the normal, negative when they overlap.
    */
    action AddContact(Vector3 normalTowardShape, Vector3 pointOnShape, number separation)
        if swapped
            reportedNormal:Set(normalTowardShape)
            // The point on the triangle is the point on the shape, moved back
            // toward the triangle by the separation.
            reportedPoint:Set(pointOnShape):MultiplyAndAdd(normalTowardShape, -separation)
        else
            reportedNormal:Set(normalTowardShape):Scale(-1)
            reportedPoint:Set(pointOnShape)
        end
        result:AddCollisionPoint(reportedNormal, reportedPoint, separation)
    end
end